        {
            "number": 6,
            "revision": "bd09f878e39c42ca4bf80c07adbd0c28ea1f6322",
            "parents": [
                "dc629a4a966149cc49eff1b9bef08efa398f43ab"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/15/79115/6",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Potin Lai",
                "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                "username": "potinlai"
            },
            "createdOn": 1746031677,
            "author": {
                "name": "Potin Lai",
                "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                "username": "potinlai"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/pldm/pldm_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why are we doing this??  We're eventually going to need pldmd in order to do code update to these devices."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/pldm/pldm_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Potin Lai",
                        "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "potinlai"
                    },
                    "message": "Due to a hardware design limitation, we\u2019ve decided to manually query the backend NICs using `pldmtool`. In my script, I stop the `pldmd` service to prevent it from interfering with EID configuration and sensor queries.\n\nHowever, we observed that pldmd is automatically restarted during host power-off events, likely triggered by the `pldmSoftPowerOff.service`.\n\nTo avoid any unintended interactions, I\u2019m only keep the `pldmtool` binary and removing or disabling the pldmd service entirely."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/pldm/pldm_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Please rearrange this to use the `pldmtool` package from this change instead of having to modify the whole recipe.  We can ensure we have only pldmtool and not pldm pulled into the image.\n\nremote:   https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/80154 pldm: split pldmtool to separate package [NEW]"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/pldm/pldm_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Potin Lai",
                        "email": "potin.lai@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "potinlai"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz, I applied this change and only include pldmtool in `OBMC_IMAGE_EXTRA_INSTALL`.\nBut the BMC image still contains pldmd & pldm-softpoweroff binaries.\n```\nOBMC_IMAGE_EXTRA_INSTALL:append = \" \\\n    pldmtool \\\n\"\n```\n\n\nI add some modification base on your changes.\n```\nPACKAGE_BEFORE_PN:append = \" ${PN}-pldmtool ${PN}-pldmd\"\nRRECOMMENDS:${PN}:append = \" ${PN}-pldmtool ${PN}-pldmd\"\n\nS = \"${WORKDIR}/git\"\nSYSTEMD_PACKAGES = \"${PN}-pldmd\"\nSYSTEMD_SERVICE:${PN}-pldmd = \"pldmd.service\"\nSYSTEMD_SERVICE:${PN}-pldmd += \"pldmSoftPowerOff.service\"\n\nFILES:${PN}-pldmtool = \"${bindir}/pldmtool\"\nFILES:${PN}-pldmd = \"${bindir}/pldmd\"\nFILES:${PN}-pldmd += \"${bindir}/pldm-softpoweroff\"\nFILES:${PN}-pldmd += \"${bindir}/set-state-effecter\"\nFILES:${PN}-pldmd += \"${bindir}/set-state-effecter-async\"\n```\n\nThen, I can success build an image only cantains pldmtool by adding `RRECOMMENDS:${PN}:remove = \"${PN}-pldmd\"` in pldm_%.bbappend at meta-catalina.\n\nCould you help check does this change also meet your expectation?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-catalina/recipes-phosphor/pldm/pldm_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "All that does is create an empty package for the base `pldm` and puts the other files into a `pldmd` package.  That shouldn't be necessary.\n\nI pushed up an update to this that I think accomplishes what we want without messing with all these FILES directives."
                }
            ],
